---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe27.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — the Full Exploration-to-Production Lifecycle" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Two Permitted Accounting Methods" },
        { id: "s4", label: "The Successful Efforts Method" },
        { id: "s5", label: "The Full Cost Method" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Depletion — the Unit-of-Production Method" },
        { id: "s7", label: "A Notable Contrast — More Comprehensive Than the International Equivalent" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Depletion Under the Unit-of-Production Method" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Expensing a Dry Exploratory Well" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IFRS 6 and US GAAP" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A specialised, industry-specific standard</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 27 governs the ACCOUNTING for OIL and GAS exploration, DEVELOPMENT, and PRODUCTION activities — a SPECIALISED, industry-SPECIFIC standard ADDRESSING a TOPIC that INTERNATIONAL standards (IFRS 6 in PARTICULAR) leave ONLY PARTIALLY addressed (Section 7).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Full Exploration-to-Production Lifecycle</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Exploration, development, and production costs</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to COSTS incurred THROUGHOUT the OIL and GAS LIFECYCLE — EXPLORATION (SEARCHING for oil/gas RESERVES), DEVELOPMENT (PREPARING proven RESERVES for PRODUCTION), and PRODUCTION (EXTRACTING the oil/GAS itself).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Two Permitted Accounting Methods</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A genuine policy choice between two established approaches</div><div class="text-supporting">ASBE No. 27 permits ENTERPRISES to CHOOSE BETWEEN the "SUCCESSFUL EFFORTS" method and the "FULL COST" method — a GENUINE accounting POLICY election, MIRRORING the SAME choice HISTORICALLY available under US GAAP (WHICH ALSO permits BOTH methods), RATHER than PRESCRIBING a SINGLE, mandatory APPROACH.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>The Successful Efforts Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Capitalise successful wells, expense unsuccessful ones</div><div class="text-supporting">UNDER the SUCCESSFUL efforts METHOD, exploration COSTS relating to WELLS that SUCCESSFULLY discover COMMERCIALLY viable RESERVES are CAPITALISED, WHILE costs RELATING to UNSUCCESSFUL ("DRY") exploratory WELLS are EXPENSED immediately — a MORE conservative approach LINKING capitalisation DIRECTLY to demonstrated SUCCESS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The Full Cost Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Capitalise all costs within a defined cost centre</div><div class="text-supporting">UNDER the FULL COST method, ALL exploration and DEVELOPMENT costs WITHIN a DEFINED geographical COST centre are CAPITALISED — REGARDLESS of WHETHER individual WELLS are SUCCESSFUL or NOT — REFLECTING the VIEW that EXPLORATION costs (INCLUDING the cost of UNSUCCESSFUL wells) are a NECESSARY part of the OVERALL cost of FINDING commercially VIABLE reserves WITHIN that COST centre.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Depletion — the Unit-of-Production Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Amortising capitalised costs based on reserves extracted</div><div class="text-supporting">CAPITALISED oil and GAS costs are DEPLETED (AMORTISED) using the UNIT-of-PRODUCTION method — BASED on the PROPORTION of ESTIMATED total PROVEN reserves EXTRACTED during the PERIOD, RATHER than a SIMPLE time-BASED depreciation SCHEDULE — REFLECTING the PATTERN in which the UNDERLYING reserve is ACTUALLY consumed.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>A Notable Contrast — More Comprehensive Than the International Equivalent</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Fuller guidance than IFRS provides</div><div class="text-supporting">INTERNATIONALLY, IFRS 6 (EXPLORATION for and EVALUATION of MINERAL resources) addresses ONLY the NARROW exploration and EVALUATION phase, LEAVING the BROADER accounting for DEVELOPMENT and PRODUCTION-phase oil/GAS activities WITHOUT a SINGLE, comprehensive IFRS standard (ENTITIES typically APPLY general PRINCIPLES from IAS 16 and IAS 38 by ANALOGY). ASBE No. 27, BY CONTRAST, provides a SINGLE, comprehensive standard COVERING the ENTIRE exploration-DEVELOPMENT-production LIFECYCLE — a GENUINELY notable CASE where China'S own domestic STANDARD offers MORE complete, DEDICATED guidance than the EQUIVALENT international FRAMEWORK.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Depletion Under the Unit-of-Production Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Amortising capitalised costs based on extraction proportion</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A capitalised oil field development cost</div><div class="wk-body">A company capitalises RMB 900,000,000 of development costs for an oil field with estimated total proven reserves of 60,000,000 barrels. During the year, 6,000,000 barrels are extracted.</div><div class="wk-answer">DEPLETION for the year = RMB 900,000,000 × (6,000,000 ÷ 60,000,000) = <strong>RMB 90,000,000</strong>, recognised as an EXPENSE REFLECTING the PROPORTION of RESERVES extracted DURING the period.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Expensing a Dry Exploratory Well</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The successful efforts method in action</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An unsuccessful exploratory well under the successful efforts method</div><div class="wk-body">A company, applying the successful efforts method, spends RMB 40,000,000 drilling an exploratory well that fails to discover commercially viable reserves.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company EXPENSES the FULL RMB 40,000,000 IMMEDIATELY, since the WELL was NOT successful — under the ALTERNATIVE full COST method, this SAME RMB 40,000,000 would INSTEAD be CAPITALISED within the RELEVANT cost CENTRE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 27 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Accounting method elected (successful efforts or full cost)</span><span>Capitalised exploration and development costs, and depletion recognised during the period</span><span>Estimated proven reserve quantities underlying the depletion calculation</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a well has discovered commercially viable reserves, under the successful efforts method</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Estimated total proven reserves, underlying the unit-of-production depletion calculation</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 6 and US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 27 vs IFRS 6 and US GAAP</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 27</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 6</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-success);">US GAAP</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Scope of coverage</span><span>Full exploration-to-production lifecycle</span><span>NARROW — exploration/evaluation phase only</span><span>Full lifecycle — comparable scope to ASBE</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Method choice</span><span>Successful efforts OR full cost</span><span>N/A — limited scope</span><span>Successful efforts OR full cost — converged with ASBE</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINE case where ASBE aligns MORE closely with US GAAP'S comprehensive TREATMENT than with the NARROWER IFRS 6.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every oil and gas event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Depletion expense</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Based on the unit-of-production method</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 4</span><span>Fixed Assets — supplies the general depreciation framework this Standard's depletion mechanics parallel</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Successful efforts method</div><div class="glossary-def">An accounting method capitalising exploration costs only for wells that discover commercially viable reserves, expensing unsuccessful wells immediately.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Full cost method</div><div class="glossary-def">An accounting method capitalising all exploration and development costs within a defined cost centre, regardless of individual well success.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe27 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
